I folded the cached-type check and profile lookup into a single path, loading `type` once and returning it directly for all invalid-profile cases. This removes redundant member loads and duplicate returns while preserving exact behavior.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 cachedType = type;

    if (cachedType == FIT_UINT8_INVALID)
    {
        const auto p = profile;
        if ((p != NULL) && (profileIndex < p->numFields))
            return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
    }

    return cachedType;
}
```